104. Image and Asset Performance
Optimise image sizes, formats and loading behaviour.
Avoid unnecessary large assets.
105. CSS and JavaScript Performance
Reduce unnecessary code and dependencies.
Use appropriate code splitting, minification and loading strategies where supported.
106. Font Performance
Load only necessary font weights and styles.
Use efficient font delivery and appropriate fallback fonts.
107. Caching and Delivery
Where supported, consider:
Browser caching.
Server caching.
CDN delivery.
Compression.
Efficient asset delivery.
Do not assume a particular hosting provider supports every optimisation.
108. Core Web Vitals
Use these targets as performance objectives:
Largest Contentful Paint (LCP): 2.5 seconds or less.
Interaction to Next Paint (INP): 200 milliseconds or less.
Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS): 0.1 or less.
These are assessment targets, not guaranteed results.
109. Performance Testing
Use suitable tools where available, including:
Lighthouse.
Google PageSpeed Insights.
WebPageTest.
Browser developer tools.
Do not invent test scores or claim an audit has been completed without performing it.
110. Performance Reporting
Distinguish between:
Estimated performance.
Development-environment measurements.
Local test results.
Production measurements.
Real-user field data.
Report the actual testing conditions.

